[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2505187465","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99778#issuecomment-2505187465","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99778","id":2505187465,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VUiCJ","user":{"login":"tetrapod00","id":145553014,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKz2dg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145553014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00","html_url":"https://github.com/tetrapod00","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-28T03:19:19Z","updated_at":"2024-11-28T03:22:45Z","body":"Is there a proposal for this? I do see https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/820 which mentions `let` but I'm not sure if this exactly implements that proposal.\r\n\r\nSee also prior implementation https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/52125.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2505187465/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2505195148","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99778#issuecomment-2505195148","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99778","id":2505195148,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VUj6M","user":{"login":"JackErb","id":16454787,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDU0Nzg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16454787?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb","html_url":"https://github.com/JackErb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-28T03:29:23Z","updated_at":"2024-12-01T01:12:20Z","body":"Addresses this proposal: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/820\r\n\r\nIt wasn't clear to me what the consensus was with this proposal, since there was so much back and forth discussion on the thread. I'm new to this process so would appreciate any guidance on how to align this change and the proposal.\r\n\r\nDifferences from the proposal:\r\n1) Use 'let' instead of 'val'. I landed on this as the most natural after reading the discussion and with my own subjective feelings towards it, coming from a Swift background\r\n2) I require an assignment at the declaration. The proposal requests allowing multiple assignments, one per branch (e.g. setting once in an if/else pair, or in each branch of a match statement). This significantly increases the complexity of the change so I avoided it\r\n3) ~~This is only for local variables. The discussion mentioned having immutable class level variables. This change doesn't include that, but I am interested in investigating further.~~","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2505195148/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2505255202","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99778#issuecomment-2505255202","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99778","id":2505255202,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VUyki","user":{"login":"ValorZard","id":7539214,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzkyMTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7539214?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValorZard","html_url":"https://github.com/ValorZard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValorZard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValorZard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValorZard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValorZard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValorZard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValorZard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValorZard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValorZard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValorZard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-28T04:47:19Z","updated_at":"2024-11-28T04:47:19Z","body":"Whats the difference between using ``let`` and using ``const``?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2505255202/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2505260807","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99778#issuecomment-2505260807","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99778","id":2505260807,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VUz8H","user":{"login":"Lazy-Rabbit-2001","id":22123964,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTIzOTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22123964?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","html_url":"https://github.com/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-28T04:54:29Z","updated_at":"2024-11-28T04:54:29Z","body":"> Whats the difference between using ``let`` and using ``const``?\n\nI think one of the nuances is that a constant should be assigned with a constant expression, while an immutable variable allows a non-constant expression.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2505260807/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2505453681","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99778#issuecomment-2505453681","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99778","id":2505453681,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VVjBx","user":{"login":"JackErb","id":16454787,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDU0Nzg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16454787?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb","html_url":"https://github.com/JackErb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-28T07:46:42Z","updated_at":"2024-11-28T07:46:42Z","body":"> Whats the difference between using `let` and using `const`?\r\n\r\nMy example is poor since you could use 'const' in that case. The difference is that const is restricted to compile-time constants, while 'let' allows you to mark any variable as immutable","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2505453681/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2505987276","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99778#issuecomment-2505987276","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99778","id":2505987276,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VXlTM","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-28T12:18:04Z","updated_at":"2024-11-28T12:18:04Z","body":"This does add additional work to all variable assignments, be they immutable or not. This will likely have a negative performance impact on all uses. In most cases it likely will be negligible, but for people doing things like procgen in GDSCript this might be a problem (as they will likely be writing to loads of variables) ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2505987276/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2506250259","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99778#issuecomment-2506250259","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99778","id":2506250259,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VYlgT","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-28T14:28:04Z","updated_at":"2024-11-28T14:28:04Z","body":"> This does add additional work to all variable assignments, be they immutable or not. This will likely have a negative performance impact on all uses. In most cases it likely will be negligible, but for people doing things like procgen in GDSCript this might be a problem (as they will likely be writing to loads of variables)\r\n\r\nWe could skip the checks in release builds to ensure the performance doesn't change in projects exported in release mode.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2506250259/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2509504802","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99778#issuecomment-2509504802","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99778","id":2509504802,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VlAEi","user":{"login":"JackErb","id":16454787,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDU0Nzg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16454787?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb","html_url":"https://github.com/JackErb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-01T01:01:40Z","updated_at":"2024-12-01T05:00:49Z","body":"Updated the review. It now supports immutable locals, function parameters, class members, and static members. Added GDScript integration tests for the parser, analyzer, and VM error messaging.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2509504802/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2509548681","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99778#issuecomment-2509548681","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99778","id":2509548681,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VlKyJ","user":{"login":"geekley","id":38332912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzMyOTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38332912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley","html_url":"https://github.com/geekley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-01T03:25:00Z","updated_at":"2024-12-01T03:25:00Z","body":"Cool! Does it work with lambdas too? Like adding `let` on lambda parameters and getting error when assigning to a `let` variable of the closure from inside the lambda code?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2509548681/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2509616209","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99778#issuecomment-2509616209","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99778","id":2509616209,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VlbRR","user":{"login":"JackErb","id":16454787,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDU0Nzg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16454787?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb","html_url":"https://github.com/JackErb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-01T07:39:20Z","updated_at":"2024-12-01T07:39:20Z","body":"> Cool! Does it work with lambdas too? Like adding `let` on lambda parameters and getting error when assigning to a `let` variable of the closure from inside the lambda code?\r\n\r\nYup, just checked, this works with lambdas :)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2509616209/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2514602094","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99778#issuecomment-2514602094","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99778","id":2514602094,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V4chu","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T13:46:43Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T13:49:47Z","body":"There is no consensus on this feature, whether it should be `readonly var`, `let` or some other keyword/annotation. Personally I prefer `let`, but @vnen disagreed as far as I remember. So my suggestions are optional for now, to avoid you doing potentially unnecessary work. I haven't reviewed this in detail, but here are a few things I noticed:\r\n\r\n1. The core probably shouldn't be touched at all. Instead of adding `property_is_immutable()` you should check for an immutability flag in `GDScript::_set()` and `GDScriptInstance::set()` (need to add the flag to the `GDScript::MemberInfo` structure instead of `PropertyInfo` usage flag). `PROPERTY_USAGE_IS_IMMUTABLE` flag might be useful for reflection, but I'd rather not add it, at least for now (since we can have max 64 flags). For documentation purposes we can add `qualifiers` field to `DocData::PropertyDoc` structure (like in `DocData::MethodDoc`). And use it in `editor_help.cpp`, `gdscript_docgen.cpp` etc. (The property setter/getter can't be found via `get_property_list()` either, although they are shown in the documentation.)\r\n2. The compiler should only report an analyzer bug when trying to generate a reassignment of an immutable variable, and the VM probably should not be affected at all (to avoid unnecessary runtime checks). If the analyzer can determine what the assignee is, then it can validate this and either produce an error, or the code is safe and the runtime check is not needed. If the analyzer cannot determine this, then the compiler will generate another opcode (`OPCODE_SET_NAMED`) and the VM will go along a generalized dynamic path, so that the runtime check will be performed in `GDScript`/`GDScriptInstance`.\r\n3. Recently, a small refactoring of the GDScript test system was done, now tracking of multiple analyzer/runtime errors is supported. Please avoid using a large number of files, try to create comprehensive tests.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2514602094/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515405429","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99778#issuecomment-2515405429","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99778","id":2515405429,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6V7gp1","user":{"login":"JackErb","id":16454787,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDU0Nzg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16454787?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb","html_url":"https://github.com/JackErb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackErb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-03T19:27:00Z","updated_at":"2024-12-03T21:27:32Z","body":"I'll avoid making any major refactors here until we reach consensus on the syntax. I still prefer the `let` syntax, and think it's worth the additional keyword to have first class immutability.\r\n\r\n> 1. The core probably shouldn't be touched at all. Instead of adding property_is_immutable() you should check for an immutability flag in GDScript::_set() and GDScriptInstance::set()\r\n\r\nThis is a good point. I did originally implement this inside of `GDScriptInstance::set()`, but I found that @export variable go through this code path when initializing and hot reloading the game. So when I naively put the immutability check in there, exported properties were no longer set to the proper value, and could not be hot reloaded. This is why I moved it into the VM layer. Putting it in the VM also makes it easier to break and display an error to the user. It might still make more sense to put the immutability check in `GDScriptInstance::set()`, but we'd need a way for @export variables to be set ignoring the immutability flag, and a way to propagate an error to the user.\r\n\r\nI'm also unsure/unaware if there's other important paths that go through `GDScriptInstance::set()` which should ignore the immutability flag.\r\n\r\n> 2. The compiler should only report an analyzer bug when trying to generate a reassignment of an immutable variable, and the VM probably should not be affected at all (to avoid unnecessary runtime checks).\r\n\r\nI think I'm doing this as you say already (besides the fact I should look into moving the check out of the VM and into `GDScriptInstance::set()`)\r\n\r\n> 3. Recently, a small refactoring of the GDScript test system was done, now tracking of multiple analyzer/runtime errors is supported. Please avoid using a large number of files, try to create comprehensive tests.\r\n\r\nNoted!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2515405429/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]